name arsenal
category Package
revision 68191
shortdesc Open Type font by Andrij Shevchenko
longdesc In 2011 Andrij's typeface became a winner of the Ukrainian Type
longdesc Design Competition "Mystetsky Arsenal" in which three main
longdesc criteria were sought for: being zeitgeist, practical, and
longdesc Ukrainian. Andrij's winning entry was crowned Arsenal and made
longdesc publicly available. Arsenal is a semi-grotesque with
longdesc traditional forms. It is primarily designed for body text and
longdesc intended for various professional communication. Its special
longdesc qualities of letter shapes and subtle contrast modulation
longdesc articulate grace and expressivity. Arsenal's somewhat lyrical
longdesc sentiment abides to the Ukrainian nature of the font. This
longdesc package provides the fonts and LaTeX support for them with
longdesc matching math. It needs LuaLaTeX or XeLaTeX.
