name bitelist
category Package
revision 25779
shortdesc Split list, in TeX's mouth
longdesc The package provides commands for "splitting" a token list at
longdesc the first occurrence of another (specified) token list. I.e.,
longdesc for given token lists s, t return b and the shortest a, such
longdesc that t = a s b. The package's mechanism differs from those of
longdesc packages providing similar features, in the following ways: the
longdesc method uses TeX's mechanism of reading delimited macro
longdesc parameters; splitting macros work by pure expansion, without
longdesc assignments; the operation is carried out in a single macro
longdesc call. A variant of the operation is provided, that retains
longdesc outer braces.
docfiles size=100
