name bxjaprnind
category Package
revision 59641
shortdesc Adjust the position of parentheses at paragraph head
longdesc In Japanese typesetting, opening parentheses placed at the
longdesc beginning of paragraphs or lines are treated specially; for
longdesc example, while the paragraph indent before normal kanji
longdesc characters is 1em, the indent before parentheses can be 0.5em,
longdesc 1em or 1.5em deoending on the local rule in effect.
