name datatool
category Package
revision 74461
shortdesc Tools to load and manipulate data
longdesc The tools comprise the packages: datatool-base.sty: the
longdesc underlying base package used by all the other packages in this
longdesc bundle; datatool.sty: databases may be created using LaTeX
longdesc commands or by importing external files; they may be sorted
longdesc numerically or alphabetically; repetitive operations (such as
longdesc mail merging) may be performed on each row of a database,
longdesc subject to conditions to exclude particular rows; commands are
longdesc provided to examine database elements, and to convert formats
longdesc (for example, to convert a numeric element to a format
longdesc compatible with l3fp or the fp package; datapie.sty: a database
longdesc may be represented as a pie chart; flexible options allow
longdesc colouring of the chart, and annotation hooks are available;
longdesc dataplot.sty: a database may be represented as a 2-dimensional
longdesc scatter or line plot; flexible options control of the plot's
longdesc overall appearance, and of legends and other extra information;
longdesc databar.sty: a database may be represented as a bar chart;
longdesc overall appearance, colouring and annotation are controllable;
longdesc datagidx.sty: provides a way of indexing or creating
longdesc glossaries/lists of abbreviations that uses TeX to do the
longdesc sorting and collating instead of using an external indexing
longdesc application, such as xindy or makeindex (although you may
longdesc prefer \printnoidxglossary now provided by the glossaries
longdesc package); databib.sty: a bibliography may be loaded into a
longdesc datatool database, and manipulated there before being printed
longdesc (this permits a LaTeX-based route to printing bibliographies in
longdesc formats for which no BibTeX style is available, although
longdesc biblatex is now the better route); and person.sty: provides
longdesc support for displaying a person's name and pronoun in a
longdesc document, thus avoiding cumbersome use of "he/she", etc. The
longdesc drawing packages make use of PGF/TikZ for their output.
longdesc Localisation support needs to be installed separately. See
longdesc datatool-regions and datatool-english. The bundle supersedes
longdesc and replaces the author's csvtools bundle.
depend fp
depend substr
depend xfor
depend xkeyval
