name datatool-english
category Package
revision 74427
shortdesc English language support for datatool.sty v3.0+
longdesc The datatool-english bundle provides English language support
longdesc for the datatool package (v3.0+). The *.ldf files should all be
longdesc placed somewhere on TeX's path. These files don't require any
longdesc explicit loading. They will automatically be input by
longdesc datatool-base.sty (or relevant supplementary package) if they
longdesc are found and required by the tracklang localisation settings.
longdesc See the datatool v3.0+ and tracklang user manuals for further
longdesc details. The English files provide encoding support for UTF-8
longdesc and ISO-8859-1 (Latin 1). Any other encoding will be treated as
longdesc US-ASCII. This bundle also includes limited support for Old
longdesc English (Anglo-Saxon) mainly to provide an example for a
longdesc language that has multiple scripts (in this case, Latin and
longdesc Runic) or for a language that has an extended Latin or
longdesc non-Latin script. The language codes are ang-Latn for
longdesc Anglo-Saxon Latin Script and ang-Runr for Anglo-Saxon Runic
longdesc Script. There's only support for UTF-8 with the Anglo-Saxon
longdesc files.
depend datatool
