name duckuments
category Package
revision 52271
shortdesc Create duckified dummy content
longdesc The package provides facilities to create duckified dummy
longdesc contents. It was inspired by the question "Getting ducks in
longdesc example images" on TeX-LaTeX Stack Exchange. The following
longdesc macros are available: \duckument[key=val] - print a short
longdesc duckument \blindduck[key=val] - print a paragraph
longdesc \ducklist(*){environment} - create a list of type environment
longdesc \ducklistlist(*){environment} - create nested lists
longdesc \duckitemize - ducklist{itemize} \duckenumerate -
longdesc ducklist{enumerate} \duckdescription - ducklist{description}
longdesc \duckumentsCreateExampleFile \duckumentsDrawRandomDucks The
longdesc package works with pdfTeX, LuaTeX, and XeTeX.
