name expex-glossonly
category Package
revision 69914
shortdesc Help gb4e, linguex, and covington users use the ExPex glossing macros
longdesc The ExPex package by John Frampton provides very fine-grained
longdesc control over glossing and example formatting, including
longdesc unlimited gloss lines and various ways of formatting multiline
longdesc glosses. By contrast the cgloss4e glossing macros provided with
longdesc gb4e, linguex, and covington, although very capable at basic
longdesc glossing, lack the degree of customization that is sometimes
longdesc needed for more complex glossing. On the other hand, for those
longdesc users who have heavily invested in using either gb4e or
longdesc linguex, or covington, shifting to ExPex can be quite daunting
longdesc and burdensome, especially since the basic syntax of the
longdesc examples is quite different. This package is an attempt to have
longdesc the best of both worlds: it allows gb4e, linguex and covington
longdesc users to keep using those packages for basic example numbering
longdesc and formatting, but also allows them to use the glossing macros
longdesc that ExPex provides.
