name kixfont
category Package
revision 18488
shortdesc A font for KIX codes
longdesc The KIX code is a barcode-like format used by the Dutch PTT to
longdesc encode country codes, zip codes and street numbers in a
longdesc machine-readable format. If printed below the address line on
longdesc bulk mailings, a discount can be obtained. The font is
longdesc distributed in Metafont format, and covers the numbers and
longdesc upper-case letters.
