name longmath
category Package
revision 71709
shortdesc Nested delimiter groups extending over multiple array cells or lines
longdesc This package provides yet another solution to some well known
longdesc typesetting problems solved in a variety of ways: multi line
longdesc formulas with paired and nested delimiters. It tackles the
longdesc problem at the Lua level, which has some advantages over
longdesc solutions implemented in TeX. In particular, the TeX code need
longdesc not be executed multiple times, and there is no interference
longdesc between TeX grouping and the nesting of delimiter groups. As a
longdesc byproduct, delimiters can be scaled in various ways, inner
longdesc delimiters come in different flavours like relational and
longdesc binary operators, punctuation symbols etc., and outer
longdesc delimiters can be selected automatically according to the
longdesc nesting level. Last but not least, delimiter groups can even
longdesc extend across several array cells or across the whole document.
longdesc A special environment is provided as well, which allows multi
longdesc line expressions to be placed inside a displayed equation and
longdesc make TeX do the line splitting and alignment.
