name luagcd
category Package
revision 68893
shortdesc Computation of gcd of integers inside LaTeX using Lua
longdesc Using Lua, the luagcd package is developped to find the
longdesc greatest common divisor (gcd) of integers in LaTeX. The package
longdesc provides commands to obtain step-by-step computation of gcd of
longdesc two integers by using the Euclidean algorithm. In addition, the
longdesc package has the command to express gcd of two integers as a
longdesc linear combination. The Bezout's Identity can be verified for
longdesc any two integers using commands in the package. No particular
longdesc environment is required for the use of commands in the package.
longdesc It is written in Lua, and the TeX file has to be compiled with
longdesc the LuaLaTeX engine.
docfiles size=28
 texmf-dist/doc/lualatex/luagcd/README.txt details="Readme"
 texmf-dist/doc/lualatex/luagcd/luagcd.pdf details="Package documentation"
 texmf-dist/doc/lualatex/luagcd/luagcd.tex
runfiles size=3
 texmf-dist/tex/lualatex/luagcd/luagcd.sty
catalogue-ctan /macros/luatex/latex/luagcd
catalogue-license lppl1.3c
catalogue-topics luatex maths
catalogue-version 1.1

