name metsymb
category Package
revision 68175
shortdesc The package provides dedicated TeX commands to generate (vectorial) meteorological symbols
longdesc The metsymb package introduces commands to generate official
longdesc meteorological symbols with vectorial quality. These include:
longdesc oktas (\zerookta, \oneokta, \twooktas, \ldots), cloud genera
longdesc (\cirrus, \cirrostratus, \nimbostratus, ...), and C_L / C_M /
longdesc C_H cloud codes (\clIII, \cmVI, \chIX, ...). Individual symbols
longdesc are designed using TikZ. They are then bundled into a dedicated
longdesc font with FontForge, and eventually tied to dedicted LaTeX
longdesc commands. The metsymb OpenType font is a side-product that can
longdesc be used on its own. This package essentially introduces a new
longdesc font in which each symbol is assigned to a glyph, which can
longdesc then be called individually from LaTeX documents via dedicated
longdesc commands.
execute addMap metsymb.map
