name multifootnote
category Package
revision 70745
shortdesc Multiple numbers for the same footnote
longdesc This package provides several commands for generating footnotes
longdesc which correspond to multiple footnote numbers (resp. marks). In
longdesc some cases, you may wish for certain footnotes to correspond to
longdesc several places in your text. The traditional solution usually
longdesc involves writing the same footnote mark multiple times at the
longdesc corresponding places. However, this approach makes it difficult
longdesc to see at once how many times a footnote has been referred to.
longdesc Therefore, the current package proposes another method: writing
longdesc the footnote marks in linear order, and allowing a footnote
longdesc text to match several of these marks.
