name ptolemaicastronomy
category Package
revision 50810
shortdesc Diagrams of sphere models for variably strict conditionals (Lewis counterfactuals)
longdesc David K. Lewis (Counterfactuals, Blackwell 1973) introduced a
longdesc sphere semantics for counterfactual conditionals. He jokingly
longdesc referred to the diagrams depicting such sphere models as
longdesc Ptolemaic astronomy, hence the name of this package. The macros
longdesc provided in this package aid in the construction of sphere
longdesc model diagrams in the style of Lewis. The macros all make use
longdesc of TikZ.
