name spelatex
category Package
revision 73664
shortdesc Create PDF documents with hyperlinks to audiofragments
longdesc This package equips the PDF that is generated with LaTeX with
longdesc hyperlinks to audio files that contain the spoken equivalent of
longdesc the original text, equations, figures and tables. The audio
longdesc files can be automatically generated using a Perl-script called
longdesc spel-wizard.pl (part of the SpeL::Wizard module available on
longdesc CPAN). This script interfaces with locally installed
longdesc text-to-speech software or with online available (paying) cloud
longdesc services to generate the audio files. To this end, the LaTeX
longdesc chunks of your text are parsed and translated to "natural
longdesc language". SpeLaTeX is babel-enabled such that your text is
longdesc read with the correct pronunciation corresponding to your
longdesc language. So far, it provides the languages English and Dutch,
longdesc but it will be extended in the future. You can package your PDF
longdesc together with the audio-files (in your favorite archive format)
longdesc and make it available to your users, such that the only
longdesc requirements to read your text and listen to the audio are a
longdesc suited PDF reader and media player. For the text-to-speech
longdesc conversion, one can use free options (festival, balabolka, ...)
longdesc or paying services (e.g. AWS polly).
