name trajan
category Package
revision 15878
shortdesc Fonts from the Trajan column in Rome
longdesc Provides fonts (both as Metafont source and in Adobe Type 1
longdesc format) based on the capitals carved on the Trajan column in
longdesc Rome in 114 AD, together with macros to access the fonts. Many
longdesc typographers think these rank first among the Roman's artistic
longdesc legacy. The font is uppercase letters together with some
longdesc punctuation and analphabetics; no lowercase or digits.
